    "title": "Auburn Police investigating stabbing at Glenn/Dean shopping center - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Elizabeth White ,\n7 hours ago\nAUBURN, Ala. (WRBL) – Auburn Police are investigating an assault on Wednesday, Sept. 10, 2025, in the 700 block of East Glenn Avenue in the Glenn/Dean shopping center.\nOpelika Police first encountered the 36-year-old male victim, who had an injury consistent with being attacked with an edged weapon. The man told officers the assault occurred in Auburn.\nHe was transported for medical treatment and is expected to recover from non-life-threatening injuries.\nPolice say no 911 calls were made from the scene before the victim was located in Opelika. Auburn officers later responded to the East Glenn location and secured the crime scene.\nInvestigators emphasize the assault was not random, but rather the result of a dispute between people who knew each other.\nDetectives confirmed the case is an isolated incident stemming from discord between the parties involved.\nThe investigation is ongoing. Anyone with information is asked to contact Auburn Police at (334) 501-3100, call/text the tip line at (334) 246-1391\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WRBL.\n8",
